From 7dc66f8fe8268a62c647e0767135b23c764bbc05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Allen <callen.23dc@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:49:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Scale drawn strings with the context's transform

String drawing placed text by the nearest translate-and-flip of the
current transform and dropped its scale, while paths took the whole
transform. Text drawn into a context with a scale came out at the
wrong size and place: Upleft renders a Mermaid diagram into a bitmap
at the screen's scale, so at 2x every label was half its size and half
as far from the diagram's corner as its box, and flowchart nodes looked
empty. The recorder now carries the transform's uniform scale beside
the translate-and-flip, and string drawing applies it to where text
goes and to its glyphs, fills and attachments.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
